{"name":"Brushed Metal","hex":"#c7c8c9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Roughened by rubbing with an abrasive brushes, especially as a finish.","Having been cleaned, tidied, or straightened with a brush.\n\n Having been processed by rotating brushes that loosen and remove dirt."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of brush"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brushed"},{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brushed metal","blocks":[{"text":"Brushed stainless steel or dull polished metal is metal with a unidirectional satin finish. It is produced by polishing the metal with a 120–180 grit belt or wheel then softening with an 80–120 grit greaseless compound or a medium non-woven abrasive belt or pad."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Brushed_Aluminium.jpg/330px-Brushed_Aluminium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brushed_metal"},{"title":"Heavy Soul (Paul Weller album)","blocks":[{"text":"Heavy Soul is the fourth solo album by English singer-songwriter Paul Weller, originally released on 23 June 1997. The album received largely favourable reviews. It sold enough to be the number one album on its week of release, however it was denied this position on a technicality – five images within the album's booklet were replaced with postcards of the images in the Special Edition release, meaning that sales of the Special Edition did not count towards the album's sales as they were defined as free gifts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Paul_weller_heavy_soul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_Soul_(Paul_Weller_album)"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Breville.jpg/500px-Breville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/